  "result": "Done! I've implemented the overdue report function. Here's what was added:\n\n**Created src/reports.js:**\n- `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` \u2014 generates an overdue invoices report\n  - Filters for 'issued' or 'partially_paid' invoices only\n  - Only includes invoices with dueDate **before** asOf (not on)\n  - Returns array of `{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }`\n  - daysOverdue = days from dueDate to asOf\n  - due = balance calculated with balanceDue\n  - **Sorted by daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)**\n  - Handles null/empty arrays gracefully\n\n**Created test/reports.test.js:**\n- 16 comprehensive test cases covering:\n  - Empty/null arrays\n  - Filtering by due date (excludes not-yet-due and exactly-due)\n  - Including issued and partially_paid, excluding draft and paid\n  - Correct daysOverdue and due calculations\n  - Proper sorting by days overdue descending\n  - Multiple scenarios with single and mixed customers\n\n**Results:**\n- All 200 tests passing (16 new report tests + 184 existing)\n- Report shows most-overdue invoices first for prioritized collections work",
